.Dd November 10, 2026
.Dt I915 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm i915
.Nd Intel Haswell graphics driver
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Cd rach2.i915
.Pp
.In drm/drm.h
.In drm/i915_drm.h
.Pp
.Pa /dev/dri/cardN
.Pp
.Pa /dev/dri/renderD Ns Ar M
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver binds the graphics device of an Intel Haswell processor with GT2
graphics, the HD 4400 of the Lenovo G50-70 (PCI 8086:0a16) among them:
the twenty device ids that Linux 6.12 gives the same device data.
It binds function 0 at 00:02.0 only, as Linux does.
.Pp
The driver binds a device only when the kernel command line has
.Cm rach2.i915 .
Without it the kernel logs the device and leaves the screen to the
firmware's framebuffer.
.Pp
A bound device is a DRM device, as
.Xr drm 4
describes, registered as
.Ql i915
with Linux's identity: description
.Ql Intel Graphics ,
version 1.6.0 and date 20230929, on the PCI bus.
It has a card node and a render node, and the features
.Dv DRIVER_GEM ,
.Dv DRIVER_RENDER ,
.Dv DRIVER_SYNCOBJ
and
.Dv DRIVER_SYNCOBJ_TIMELINE .
It does not yet set modes, so it has neither
.Dv DRIVER_MODESET
nor
.Dv DRIVER_ATOMIC ,
as Linux's i915 on a device without display.
.Pp
At bind the driver maps the registers, the first 2 MiB of BAR 0,
uncached; turns on memory decoding and bus mastering; masks, disables and
clears every interrupt source of the display engine, the GT, power
management and the south display; then takes a vector and enables the
device's MSI message on it.
A machine without message vectors leaves the device without interrupts,
which nothing needs yet.
The kernel logs
.Dq i915: found
with the device's place, id, subplatform and revision, and
.Dq i915: registered
with its card.
.Sh IOCTLS
The core's ioctls are those of
.Xr drm 4 .
The driver's own,
.Dv DRM_IOCTL_I915_*
from
.Dv DRM_COMMAND_BASE ,
fall in the families below.
.Ss Identity and parameters
.Dv DRM_IOCTL_VERSION
answers as above.
.Dv DRM_IOCTL_I915_GETPARAM
and
.Dv DRM_IOCTL_I915_SETPARAM
are not yet served and fail with
.Er EINVAL .
.Ss Buffers
.Dv DRM_IOCTL_I915_GEM_CREATE ,
the mapping, domain, caching, tiling, busy and wait calls are not yet
served and fail with
.Er EINVAL .
.Ss Contexts
.Dv DRM_IOCTL_I915_GEM_CONTEXT_CREATE
and the context calls are not yet served and fail with
.Er EINVAL .
.Ss Submission
.Dv DRM_IOCTL_I915_GEM_EXECBUFFER2
and its variants are not yet served and fail with
.Er EINVAL .
.Ss Display
Mode setting is not yet served; see above.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /dev/dri/renderDM
.It Pa /dev/dri/cardN
The card node of a bound device.
.It Pa /dev/dri/renderD Ns Ar M
Its render node.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr backlight 4 ,
.Xr drm 4 ,
.Xr watchdog 4
.Sh HISTORY
The driver follows Linux 6.12's i915, whose register names and device
table it takes.
